    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\nYour Sub-Research Questions are well defined. You took a small scope, and formulated open questions"
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "Your schedule is very thorough"
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "You present the important limitation of your methodology (being constrained to secondary sources only) well"
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "Weaknesses:",
    "attributes": {
      "bold": true
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\nThe methodology section should clearly show how you plan to address and answer all of your (sub-)research questions. A literature review makes sense, but you treat all of your research questions the same and stay quite superficial. Think about treating your SRQs individually (even if they get to a similar methodology as a result), as it also shows to the reader you have thought about all SRQs and present how you will tackle them"
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "Already the main RQ should have a certain scope such that it can be answered in your thesis. Your RQ is really broad, and cannot possibly be answered fully in a thesis. Take inspiration in your SRQs and narrow down the main RQ already (and possibly not all four SRQs are relevant if the scope becomes too wide)"
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "There should be a coherent citation style that fits into the written text. Your references to [1], [2] etc in the middle of the text are usually not good practice. If the latex template doesnt provide you with a different citation style, cite differently and put the references after your sentences, not in the middle"
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The theoretical framework should be correct by itself. \"HCI\" is not a set of design principles, but the name of a discipline. Become more precise in your language and use citations in this paragraph to assure good scientific writing"
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "Combining different existing work should help the overall structure and motivation of your expose, showing a clear gap in SOTA and justifying the necessity of your research. Your SOTA section includes different sources, but doesn't combine them in a meaningful way. When you write the SOTA section, try to build a comprehensive image for the reader such that it clearly leads towards your research."
  },
  {
    "retain": 1,
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  }
